":"gcp.run.services.authentication","l":"full","t":"Authentication (allow unauthenticated / IAM invoker)","x":[]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.services.scaling_billing","l":"full","t":"Service scaling, ingress and CPU allocation (request-based / instance-based billing)","x":["Billing is not metered; the console mirrors the cpuIdle setting but Vyomi does not charge for instance time."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.services.source","l":"limited","t":"Source (inline function entry point, runtime, code)","x":["\"Save and redeploy\" is enforced, not just stored: a source/runtime/entry-point edit changes the revision's image fingerprint, so the same revision-diff logic the Admin API uses for any template change cuts a real new revision (visible on the Revisions tab, traffic following it) exactly as a redeploy would."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.get"],"id":"gcp.run.services.yaml","l":"limited","t":"YAML view of the service config","x":["The YAML view is generated read-only from the real service state; editing and re-applying YAML directly is not simulated — use the other tabs."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.run.services.continuous_deployment","l":"not_simulated","t":"Continuously deploy from a repository (Cloud Build / GitHub) or set up continuous deployment on an existing service","x":["Continuous deployment needs a real GitHub/Cloud Source Repository connection and a real container build (Cloud Build). The simulator has no git-hosting service to fetch source from, and shared cores forbid network egress (tests/conformance/test_no_cloud_egress.py) — there is nothing local to connect to or build, unlike a stateful sub-resource this appliance could model on its own."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.create (simulator-only sub-resource)","projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.list","projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.delete","pubsub.projects.topics.publish"],"id":"gcp.run.services.triggers","l":"limited","t":"Event triggers (Eventarc) and Cloud Build source deploys","x":["Modelled as a Pub/Sub-transport Eventarc trigger (a service sub-resource, since Vyomi has no eventarc.googleapis.com): \"Add trigger\" binds the service to an existing Pub/Sub topic, and publishing on that topic — from the Pub/Sub console, the native wire, or any other trigger that publishes — really invokes the destination service once per message (the trigger's service account is implicitly a run.invoker; a direct :invoke enforces the IAM invoker policy) and writes a real Cloud Logging entry read back on the Observability tab. The Functions console's services/{s}/triggers path is the same Trigger resource."]},{"a":["logging.entries.write","logging.entries.list"],"id":"gcp.run.services.observability","l":"limited","t":"Observability (request metrics, container instance count, logs)","x":["Vyomi does not run the deployed container and does not meter real HTTP request traffic, so there are no request-count/latency time series or container instance metrics to show."]},{"a":["projects.locations.jobs.create","projects.locations.jobs.get","projects.locations.jobs.list","projects.locations.jobs.delete","projects.locations.jobs.run"],"id":"gcp.run.jobs.crud","l":"full","t":"Jobs (create, list, run, delete)","x":[]},{"a":["projects.locations.jobs.get"],"id":"gcp.run.jobs.yaml","l":"limited","t":"YAML view of the job config","x":["The YAML view is generated read-only from the real job state; editing and re-applying YAML directly is not simulated."]},{"a":["logging.entries.write","logging.entries.list"],"id":"gcp.run.jobs.observability","l":"limited","t":"Job observability (execution metrics, logs)","x":["Metrics are real, derived from this job's own execution history (executions/succeeded/failed/task counts), not metered container resource usage — Vyomi runs each task to completion synchronously, so there are no per-task CPU/memory/duration series."]},{"a":["projects.locations.jobs.run"],"id":"gcp.run.jobs.triggers","l":"limited","t":"Job triggers (Eventarc, Cloud Scheduler bindings shown on the job)","x":["A Cloud Scheduler trigger is ENFORCED, not just displayed: \"Add trigger\" creates a Cloud Scheduler job whose httpTarget names this job's own Admin API v2 :run endpoint, and when that scheduler job fires (on its cron schedule, or via \"Run now\") the appliance's httpTarget delivery really calls jobs.run — a new execution starts, exactly like a real OIDC-authenticated Cloud Scheduler → Cloud Run Jobs binding."]},{"a":["projects.locations.workerPools.create","projects.locations.workerPools.get","projects.locations.workerPools.list","projects.locations.workerPools.delete"],"id":"gcp.run.workerpools.crud","l":"full","t":"Worker pools (create, list, delete)","x":["Worker pool instance splits across revisions are not modelled; a worker pool always runs its current template."]},{"a":["domainmappings.create","domainmappings.get","domainmappings.list","domainmappings.delete"],"id":"gcp.run.domainmappings.crud","l":"full","t":"Domain mappings (map a custom domain to a service, DNS records)","x":["Vyomi does not provision a real TLS certificate or serve traffic on the mapped domain; the DNS records it returns are illustrative."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.template.autoscaling","l":"limited","t":"Autoscaling factors (target utilization, concurrency)","x":["The autoscaling rule (desired instances from in-flight requests, concurrency target, CPU target, min/max) is computed and validated, but Vyomi runs no real instance fleet: invocations are served in-process, so instance counts shown are the autoscaler's decision, not running containers."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.template.health-checks","l":"limited","t":"Startup and liveness probes","x":["Probe definitions are validated against the real Cloud Run rules (one handler, period/timeout/threshold bounds) and stored; Vyomi does not run a container, so probes are never executed and a failing probe never restarts an instance."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.template.volumes","l":"limited","t":"Volumes and volume mounts (in-memory, Secret Manager, Cloud Storage, NFS)","x":["Volumes and mounts are validated (unique names, one source, absolute and unique mount paths, referenced bucket exists, second-generation requirements) and stored; no filesystem is actually mounted into a container."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create"],"id":"gcp.run.template.ephemeral-disk","l":"limited","t":"Ephemeral disk (emptyDir on disk with a size limit)","x":["Requires the second-generation execution environment and a size limit as on the real service; the disk is not allocated, since Vyomi runs no container."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.jobs.create"],"id":"gcp.run.template.cloudsql","l":"limited","t":"Cloud SQL connections","x":["Connection names are validated and each must name a Cloud SQL instance that exists in Vyomi; the /cloudsql unix-socket proxy is not started, connect to the instance's own endpoint instead."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create"],"id":"gcp.run.template.cmek","l":"limited","t":"Customer-managed encryption key (CMEK)","x":["The key must be a CryptoKey in the same region that exists in Vyomi; revision data is not actually encrypted with it, and revoking the key does not stop instances."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.create","projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.binary-authorization","l":"config_only","t":"Binary Authorization","x":["The setting (default policy or a named policy) is validated and stored, but Vyomi has no attestation service, so images are never blocked at deploy time."]},{"a":["projects.locations.services.patch"],"id":"gcp.run.services.revision-tags","l":"limited","t":"Revision tags","x":["Tags give a revision a dedicated tagged URL and are validated (format, uniqueness) and returned in trafficStatuses; the wildcard tagged URL is served by Vyomi's own endpoint, not a public DNS name."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.run.gpu","l":"not_simulated","t":"GPU for Cloud Run services and jobs (NVIDIA L4)","x":["Cloud Run GPUs attach NVIDIA L4 hardware to a container instance; Vyomi runs containers on the host Docker engine with no GPU passthrough or scheduler."]},{"a":["services.create","services.patch","revisions.get"],"id":"gcp.run.networking","l":"limited","t":"Networking (HTTP/2 end-to-end, session affinity, VPC egress, service mesh, custom audiences)","x":["These are validated configuration on the revision/service, enforced and round-tripped like the real Cloud Run Admin API v2: ports[].name http1/h2c (one port, ingress container only), sessionAffinity, vpcAccess (connector in the same region that must exist in the VPC core, or one Direct VPC interface whose subnetwork must exist, egress ALL_TRAFFIC / PRIVATE_RANGES_ONLY, network tags), serviceMesh resource name, and customAudiences."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.run.source-deploy-ar","l":"not_simulated","t":"Source deploy pushes the BuildKit image into Artifact Registry (cloud-run-source-deploy)","x":["Offline: a connected-repo source deploy builds the Dockerfile on BuildKit, pushes the image into the simulated Artifact Registry repository cloud-run-source-deploy (created on demand, as gcloud does) and cuts the revision with that Artifact Registry reference. Vyomi still does not run the container for arbitrary images; no buildpacks."]}],"id":"run","ops":41,"registry_unreachable":[["gcp.run.services.triggers","projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.create (simulator-only sub-resource)"],["gcp.run.services.triggers","projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.list"],["gcp.run.services.triggers","projects.locations.services.eventarcTriggers.delete"],["gcp.run.domainmappings.crud","domainmappings.create"],["gcp.run.domainmappings.crud","domainmappings.get"],["gcp.run.domainmappings.crud","domainmappings.list"],["gcp.run.domainmappings.crud","domainmappings.delete"]],"title":"Cloud Run","total":59}
